Your job is to define a scope that can be treated COMPREHENSIVELY and AUTHORITATIVELY at the target
length — the standard is a Nature Review or a "Very Short Introduction" volume, not a summary.

First assess breadth. If the topic is too large to cover this deeply (e.g. it spans several fields
or decades of research), NARROW it to a specific, tractable sub-question and move the rest to
`out_of_scope`. Do not widen scope to fill a word count; prefer depth over breadth. State the
reasoning in `scope_rationale`, and record the narrowing under `out_of_scope`/`assumptions`.

Produce a single sharpened `refined_question`, 4–8 decomposable `sub_questions`, explicit
`in_scope` and `out_of_scope` lists, the audience, `assumptions`, the `length_preset`, and a short
`scope_rationale` explaining why this scope admits authoritative depth at the target length.
